diff --git a/docs/spec_performance.md b/docs/spec_performance.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1c2016e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/spec_performance.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# RSpec performance optimization
+
+## Model spec baseline
+
+Run:
+
+```text
+bundle exec rspec spec/models --format progress --profile 30
+```
+
+- Baseline: 1,795 examples in 199.2 seconds (3m19.2s), 0 failures.
+- Baseline seed: 43000.
+- Files took 3.18 seconds to load.
+- Optimized pass: 1,795 examples in 118.029 seconds (1m55.93s), 0 failures.
+- Optimized seed: 63075.
+- Files took 1.73 seconds to load.
+- Wall-time improvement: 40.7% (`(199.2 - 118.029) / 199.2`).
+
+The focused changes exceed the 30-35% model-spec target.
+
+## Shared setup changes
+
+- Loaded TestProf's `let_it_be` recipe and used it for repeated, stable setup records in the slow model example groups. Shared records use `reload: true, freeze: false` so mutations are isolated while setup stays reusable.
+- Shared the account-status cleanup fixture set and its media/pin/favourite/bookmark setup across examples with `let_it_be` and `before_all`.
+- Shared setup across the public-feed, tag-feed, notification pagination, threading, trend-tags, and trend-statuses example groups.
+- Moved Sidekiq's default to suite setup. Sidekiq fake mode is now an around-hook selected by `:sidekiq_fake` metadata instead of running `Sidekiq.testing!(:inline)` before every example.
+- Skipped route reloading and DNS stubbing for model examples; both were repeated on setup paths that model specs do not need.
+- Kept per-example Rails cache and Redis cleanup in `spec/rails_helper.rb`. An early Redis/cache tag experiment leaked state in feed, trend, and account examples, so the global cleanup was restored.
+
+## Profile observations
+
+Baseline slow example groups included:
+
+- `Trends::Statuses` at 18.37 seconds across 12 examples.
+- `AccountStatusesCleanupPolicy` at 22.22 seconds across 36 examples.
+- `Status::ThreadingConcern` at 9.23 seconds across 16 examples.
+- `Status::FetchRepliesConcern` at 6.97 seconds across 15 examples.
+- `TagFeed` at 14.10 seconds across 33 examples.
+- `PublicFeed` at 11.12 seconds across 43 examples.
+- `Notification` at 7.93 seconds across 25 examples.
+
+The optimized profile is led by trend refreshes and media attachment metadata. No model spec failed in the final pass.
+
+## Future request-spec phase
+
+Before changing request specs, establish a separate baseline with only:
+
+```text
+bundle exec rspec spec/requests --format progress --profile 30
+```
+
+Do not run system or streaming specs, and do not run the complete suite or whole spec directories at once. Keep factory changes out of this phase; revisit factories only after the model and request phases.
+
+## Scope
+
+No app runtime code or factory files were changed. The optimization is limited to RSpec configuration and model-spec setup/assertion-preserving refactoring.
